'FNIS ini file
'
'IMPORTANT: To take effect, this file (FNIS.ini0) has to be copied MANUALLY to Skyrim\Data\FNIS.ini. Then edit FNIS.ini.
'For NMM Virtual Install or MO users: FNIS.ini has to go to "real" SKYRIM\Data (NOT inside the virtual mod folders!) 
'Note: All lines starting with ' are comments. To activate a parameter you have to remove the apostrophe (e.g. "PSCD=1")
'
'PSCD implements "Proper Spell Cast Direction" fix based on www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/68794
'That allows the player to cast spells or shoot arrows even if the target is VERY well above or below
'Downside: when using camera mods or certain animation replacers, the bending might look unnatural
'Users who want the vanilla bend limits rather then the PSCD fix can switch this fix off here (PSCD=0)
'Default PSCD=0 (DO NOT use "Proper Spell Cast Direction")
'
'PSCD=1
'
'File Redirection allows you to put FNIS generated files into a separate folder (should be outside of the Skyrim "Data")
'This supports different profiles in MO (and Vortex?)
'The following parameter defines the root directory for the resultant files. For example
'Default (no file redirection possible)
'
'RedirectFiles=D:\___FNIS_Redirect
'
'Instant Execution will run FNIS without having to click either "Update FNIS Behavior" or "Exit".
'The FNIS window will only pop up if FNIS has to report error or warnings. 
'This is a feature primarily for Vortex, but can be used otherwise.
'It is recommended that you use this feature only from a windows .bat file, because otherwise you will not see when FNIS is done.
'Default (regular windows operation)
'
'InstantExecute=1
'
'Load CTD Calculation (only FNIS XXL) calculates the "animation" space used by the current FNIS installation and each of its 
'FNIS depending to determine if the game will CTD on load. See https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/articles/1168.
'If you don't want this information (e.g when you use one of the SKSE plugins that fix the responsible Skyrim bug)
'you can switch it off (LoadCTDCalculation=0)
'See SKSE plugins Animation Limit Crash Fix SSE (Skyrim SE and LE), SSE Engine Fixes (Skyrim SE only)
'Default: LoadCTDCalculation=1 (Calculation on, XXL only)
'
'LoadCTDCalculation=0